# EAS Build archives from the GIT ROOT, and this repo holds five independent
# projects under one .git (backend, frontend, showcase-website, marketing, mobile)
# with NO npm workspaces. So `eas build` from mobile/ was uploading the ENTIRE repo
# (~379 MB) when the mobile app alone is a few MB. Keep only mobile/.
#
# NOTE: when a .easignore exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore for the upload,
# so the per-project ignores (node_modules, build output) are re-listed below or
# they would be swept right back in.

# Ignore every top-level entry in the repo…
/*

# …except the mobile app (the only thing the mobile build needs).
!/mobile/

# Within the mobile app, drop dependencies + build output + caches — these are
# installed / regenerated on the EAS build servers and must not be uploaded.
/mobile/node_modules/
/mobile/.expo/
/mobile/dist/
/mobile/web-build/
/mobile/ios/
/mobile/android/
/mobile/*.log
/mobile/.DS_Store
